**Verdict: approve.** No High or Medium findings against T25’s harness contract.

- **Low — restore does not prove resumed delivery.** [realtime-stream-faults-probe.spec.ts:280](E:/projects/virtual-off
ice/__tests__/api/playwright/messaging-phase5/realtime-stream-faults-probe.spec.ts:280) accepts `SUBSCRIBED` without 
checking server-confirmed streaming or a fresh event. A successful join followed by a replication failure could still 
produce the recorded recovery result. **Smallest fix:** for streams that recover, call `waitForReady()` and verify one 
new B event after restore.

- **Low — status observations aggregate watched pages.** [realtime-stream-faults.ts:617](E:/projects/virtual-office/__t
ests__/api/playwright/helpers/realtime-stream-faults.ts:617) filters statuses only by stream and sequence; readiness 
can combine a callback from one watched tab with a joined channel on another socket. **Smallest fix:** add 
page/conversation selectors to status waits, or explicitly restrict channel-specific assertions to one watched 
page/socket. The current probe enforces one A socket, so this does not invalidate its matrix.

The fault mechanisms fit D4’s permitted Phoenix frame shaping: real joins reach Supabase, and actual SDK subscription 
callbacks produce the statuses. The injected error reply operates at the protocol boundary. The invalid-token push 
invokes a real, channel-local server shutdown. Playwright’s `connectToServer()` retains a real server connection while 
intercepting messages. [Playwright 
documentation](https://playwright.dev/docs/api/class-websocketroute#web-socket-route-connect-to-server), [pinned 
Realtime implementation](https://github.com/supabase/realtime/blob/v2.112.6/lib/realtime_web/channels/realtime_channel.
ex#L485-L548).

The current probe’s delivery checks are substantive: exact message IDs, the group’s conversation-update frame, typing 
broadcasts, application effects, and post-fault Presence events. No cross-topic fault path was found for the current 
topics, heartbeat traffic, token-refresh pushes, or harness references. Device-context closure also bounds 
server-channel lifetime between tests. The added product trace logs only a fixed channel label and status under the 
existing debug gate; production can enable that gate explicitly.

Approval is scoped to T25. Its timeout cells genuinely reach the SDK’s `TIMED_OUT`, but first receive `CHANNEL_ERROR`; 
timeout-first recovery remains unproved. Private typing is matched by the harness but untested by this probe. T15 must 
verify its broadcast-only private topic and distinguish authentication/access-loss closure from recoverable closure. 
The list/typing streams remaining `CLOSED` after restore document today’s missing application recovery; AC-015 
recovery remains T13/T15 work.

Retained JSON and text corroborate three consecutive **18/18** runs starting **05:19:01, 05:30:30, and 05:41:57 UTC**, 
each with Chrome 9 and Edge 9, zero retries, flakes, or skips. Regression records show **102/102**; both discarded 
non-vacuity controls fail at the intended assertions. Current source timestamps and test titles are consistent with 
those runs.

Independent static checks pass: type-check, product diff check, and ESLint with **0 errors / 8 pre-existing 
warnings**. Review remained read-only; no database access, Playwright run, or dev server was started.
